Spec: Aikana
Platform: Python/FastHTML/HTMX/SQLite/Tailwind CSS

Purpose:
  Aikana is a time-keeping and lesson calendar. A single admin (the teacher) records courses, course realizations,
  lessons and holidays. Unauthenticated students can only view the data. The calendar is presented as a semester
  wall planner and as a per-CourseRealization weekly calendar.

Structure:
  ./src/aikana/: the application package, with its entry point and feature packages for the domain entities,
    calendar views and auth
  ./tests/: automated tests
  ./data/: local-only directory mounted into the container at `/data`
  ./README.md: how to launch the app
  ./CONTRIBUTE.md: how to develop iteratively with SpecDD
  ./Dockerfile: multi-stage image definition shared by local testing and production
  ./docker-compose.yml: local run configuration that builds the `dev` stage and mounts `./data` at `/data`
  ./pyproject.toml: package metadata, dependencies and tool configuration
  ./uv.lock: locked dependency versions produced by `uv`

Owns:
  ./pyproject.toml
  ./uv.lock
  ./README.md
  ./CONTRIBUTE.md
  ./Dockerfile
  ./docker-compose.yml
  ./.dockerignore
  ./.gitignore

References:
  ./src/aikana/architecture.sdd

Must:
  The SQLite database file lives at `/data/app.db` so that it can be mounted as a persistent volume.
  The admin password is read from the `ADMIN_PASSWORD` environment variable and the listening port from `PORT`.
  Unauthenticated visitors can view all data and cannot create, change or delete anything.
  Only the authenticated admin can write data.
  All UI text is in English.
  Tailwind CSS is delivered through the Play CDN script, so no Node build step exists.
  Dependencies are declared in `pyproject.toml` and locked in `uv.lock`, and every Docker stage installs exactly the
  locked set with `uv`.
  `Dockerfile` has a `base` stage with the common setup, a `dev` stage and a `prod` stage that both inherit from
  `base`. `prod` is the last stage, so a plain `docker build` produces the production image, and it installs no
  development dependencies.
  `docker-compose.yml` builds the `dev` stage through `target: dev`.
  The container starts the app with `python -m aikana.main`, so no `Procfile` exists.
  The repository root contains no application source files.
  Development proceeds in small increments and every increment is tested locally in Docker first.

Must not:
  Nothing in the repository or its tooling may publish, push or deploy to Dokku or GitHub. The human decides when and
  how to do that.
  Secrets, including `ADMIN_PASSWORD` values and database files, must not be committed.

Forbids:
  Any database other than SQLite.
  Any ORM other than `fastlite`'s MiniDataAPI Spec implementation, as detailed in ./src/aikana/architecture.sdd.
  Frontend frameworks other than HTMX and Tailwind CSS.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Scaffold `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yml`, `.dockerignore`, `requirements.txt`, `Procfile`, `.gitignore` and a minimal `main.py` that serves a page on `$PORT`
  [x] #2 Update README.md run instructions to match the working Docker setup
  [x] #3 Decide how the six-month semester range is chosen, then reflect it in ./src/aikana/semester/semester.sdd
  [ ] #4 Implement feature packages in order, following ./src/aikana/architecture.sdd: ./src/aikana/shared/shared.sdd, ./src/aikana/auth/auth.sdd, ./src/aikana/courses/courses.sdd, ./src/aikana/semester/semester.sdd, ./src/aikana/holidays/holidays.sdd, ./src/aikana/realizations/realizations.sdd, ./src/aikana/lessons/lessons.sdd, ./src/aikana/day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd
  [x] #5 Restructure into `src/aikana` and `tests`, and migrate dependencies from `requirements.txt` to `uv` and `pyproject.toml`
  [x] #6 Drop `Procfile` and restructure `Dockerfile` into `base`, `dev` and `prod` stages, with `docker-compose.yml` targeting `dev`
  [x] #7 Build a hardcoded first-pass visual semester view (one Semester, two placeholder Courses, two placeholder CourseRealizations, placeholder Lessons, one placeholder Holiday) ahead of full persistence, per the Tasks in ./src/aikana/shared/shared.sdd, ./src/aikana/courses/courses.sdd, ./src/aikana/semester/semester.sdd, ./src/aikana/realizations/realizations.sdd, ./src/aikana/lessons/lessons.sdd and ./src/aikana/holidays/holidays.sdd

Done when:
  The app starts in local Docker with `ADMIN_PASSWORD` set and serves both calendar views.
  Data written by the admin survives a container restart through the `./data` volume.
  `uv run pytest` passes.
  `specdd lint` passes.
